  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kosovo Energy Security of Supply (KESS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives for Kosovo: The Kosovo Energy Security of Supply (KESS) project provides technical assistance across the Kosovo energy sector, primarily to the Ministry of Economic Development (MED), for the design and implementation of energy security projects in the country. The activity will strengthen the Government of Kosovo&#x2019;s (GOK) continuing efforts to modernize the country&#x2019;s existing electricity sector, and build the capacity of the GOK to negotiate and implement future energy sector transactions in order to provide for a more reliable, cleaner, and affordable electric energy supply.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kosovo Energy Security of Supply activity will improve Kosovo&apos;s energy security by building the capacity of the Ministry of Economic Development and providing a full range of long-term and quick response professional services across the Kosovo energy sector, with a focus on new power generation. Assistance will provide advisory services necessary to attract investments and manage large scale energy sector transactions using international best practices for the design and implementation of energy security projects in the country, beginning with private sector investment in new power generation (Kosovo C). The assistance will help the Government of Kosovo move from commercial close towards financial close on the vital Kosovo C project.</narrative>
  </description>
